= Exercise 1
== Question 1
The null hypothesis is $H_0: mu >= 8%$
and the alternative hypothesis is $H_1: mu < 8%$

== Question 2
The type of test that should be used here is a one-sided test (less than).
This is because we only care about testing in one direction,
not about testing if there is a difference

= Exercise 2
== Question 1
The null hypothesis for testing whether the training has an effect on stress level is
$H_0: mu_("before") = mu_("after")$
and the alternative hypothesis is
$H_1: mu_("before") != mu_("after")$.

== Question 2
"Rejecting $H_0$" in this example implies that the mindfulness training program has an effect on the average stress level.
However it does not indicate if the stress level increases or decreases.
